      "last_decision": {
        "at": "2026-10-20T16:51:21.557919+00:00",
        "symbol": "GOOG",
        "action": "hold",
        "summary": "Stay flat on GOOG.NAS. This second research round upgraded the FY25 10-K from publisher-level to primary-source: 2025 capex $91.4B with management guiding a 'significant increase' in 2026 infrastructure investment (76dee2db466cdecb), Cloud operating income $13.9B on $58.7B revenue (~24% margin, roughly doubled from $6.1B on $43.2B), Services operating income +$18.1B, OCF $164.7B, offset by widening Alphabet-level AI R&D losses ($10.5B to $16.8B) and Other Bets losses ($4.4B to $7.5B) (89486494f4e19f73, b6705da43122f43f, 9cfaceb8c7d9d4c9). It also verified the measurement-alternative private-stake book rose $35.2B to $64.1B during 2025 with $45.6B remeasured on unobservable inputs (a4c7919f6aeaee02) - confirming large non-cash OI&E swings as a structural feature, not a one-off. The unresolved dispute persists: Q2 capex $44.9B exceeded Q2 OCF $39.1B, $49.6B was raised in common plus 6.25% mandatory convertible preferred, and the $195-205B FY26 capex guide still rests on unverified publisher summaries. The decisive number - Q3 Cloud segment operating income versus the depreciation wave - remains unfiled; the earnings date is still not 8-K-confirmed. The tape gives no edge: fresh quote 337.51/337.56, drift lower within the 333-351 Bollinger band (live packet), RSI ~48.5, negative MACD histogram, ATR ~7.9 - not the decisive volume-confirmed close below the dated 200-session mean (~339.26) that the invalidation trigger requires. Holding cash remains the correct resolution of an unresolved, primary-evidenced dispute.",
        "thesis": "Watch stance carried forward, now strengthened by primary-source verification of the 10-K baseline. Verified facts cut both ways: demand is real and accelerating (revenue $402.8B FY25 +15.1%, Cloud margin ~24% and doubled, Services operating income $139.4B, $513.9B Cloud backlog per prior filings), while the capital cycle is verified as well (2025 capex $91.4B, +74% YoY, with explicit management language that 2026 investment will significantly increase and that depreciation, energy and network costs will rise with AI serving - 76dee2db466cdecb). The equity/hybrid funding choice is verified: $49.6B net proceeds including $19.0B of 6.25% cumulative mandatory convertible preferred plus a $40B ATM, expressly for AI/compute capex (280f6fb11eb215ec). Earnings-quality caveat is now structural: the $64.1B measurement-alternative book with unobservable inputs means GAAP EPS can whipsaw on mark reversals without cash effect (a4c7919f6aeaee02). Macro is unchanged: DGS10 5.10% vs 2Y 4.77% is term-premium/real-rate pressure, not a policy signal (DFEDTARU 4.0%); VIX ~20 and HY spreads 3.31% show repricing, not distress (c82957760f866e9c, 4c6c610ef1195bcb, 8105bdd1c466d7ce, b9d7d8ce511c320e) - so there is no rate-relief catalyst and any upside must be earnings-carried. Today's secondary news (BofA Cloud/TPU upside note, tech-led selling on AI fears, UK Cloud outage, Meta Oct-21 print) is thesis-neutral pending primary verification. Neither the bull nor bear case is falsified; the falsification point is the Q3-26 10-Q segment data. Six hours is an ordinary minimum; paying for either hypothesis pre-print remains uneconomic.",
        "countercase": "Bulls argue the show-me discount is the entry: the bar is reset low after the ~6% post-Q2 drop despite strong Cloud results, BofA flags Q3 Cloud/TPU upside, Cloud margin has already nearly doubled once and the $513.9B backlog (over half convertible within 24 months) verifies contracted demand; the 200-session mean has held at ~339 with only a -3.1% 20-session pullback inside a +35% 12-month trend, credit is calm, and waiting forfeits gap optionality if the Q3 print discloses Cloud margin absorbing the depreciation wave. Bears counter that at a 5.10% 10Y and 5.43% 30Y with no rate-relief catalyst, ~$200B capex funded by equity, mandatory converts and serial dilution before ROI is proven compresses ROIC and multiples; the $77.4B Q2 unrealized OI&E mark could reverse and cut GAAP EPS; peer AI-financing fears (CoreWeave) and Meta's Oct-21 print could de-rate the whole complex before Alphabet reports; and today's drift to 337.5 with a weak 0.78x-volume bounce shows no demand confirmation. Both cases remain credible; neither is confirmed by primary Q3 evidence.",
        "invalidation": "The watch stance resolves to action on specific events: (1) Q3-26 10-Q filing - extract Cloud segment operating income versus the nearly doubled depreciation run-rate, any filed capex guidance replacing the unverified $195-205B publisher figure, diluted share count, and like-for-like backlog growth; (2) earnings date confirmed via an official 8-K rather than social posts; (3) verified scope, duration and issuer statement on the Oct-20 Google Cloud outage; (4) Meta's Oct-21 results as the hyperscaler capex read-across; (5) price evidence - a decisive close below the dated 200-session mean (~339.26 on the Oct-19 series) on above-average volume, or a range breakout above ~351 with Cloud-positive primary confirmation. The current 337.51/337.56 quote sits marginally below that dated reference but the live packet's 60-session window yields no 200-day calculation, so treat the trigger as requiring the dated-series comparison plus volume confirmation; today's drift is routine range movement. A close action would require an owned position whose thesis a new filing or verified event specifically invalidates; no position exists. Full-filing certification remains incomplete - disclosed and owner-authorized for this demo experiment - which further justifies no directional exposure before primary Q3 numbers.",
